H6 (SECONDARY) mixed-effects slope over 11 scales, 95 paired points:
    PRIMARY (regression on 11 scale means): slope -0.0127 95% CI [-0.0291,+0.0037] p=0.1138
      => CI SPANS ZERO: direction is scale-consistent but the effect is NOT resolved as scale-varying.
    sensitivity (same slope, different unit of analysis):
      cluster_by_scale       -0.0126 CI[-0.0236,-0.0016] n=11 (scale)
      cluster_by_seed        -0.0126 CI[-0.0181,-0.0071] n=15 (seed (anticonservative))
      mixedlm_seed_prereg    FAILED: Singular matrix
    !! ESTIMATORS DISAGREE on whether the CI covers zero. The primary (scale-level) reading governs;
       the paper must report the magnitude as UNRESOLVED and state that the seed-clustered
       interval is anticonservative for a scale-level question.

NOTE: n=15 per cell. We report effect sizes with bootstrap CIs and flag
when a CI crosses zero (sign unresolved). Claims are restricted to the
tested regime (<=50M+ non-embed params, 20M tokens, GPT-2 BPE); broader
scale is explicitly out of scope and listed under Limitations.
